{"id":45765,"ord":105,"n_segments":146,"prev":45764,"next":45766,"doc":{"id":"56679","title":"56679_Arthur Briggs oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Arthur Briggs","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/56679/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=56679"},"chapter":"Bricktop's, Armstrong and the Harlemites","title":"Personnel and origin of Freddy Johnson's Harlemites","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Briggs lists the Harlemites, built on Bricktop's band by Freddy Johnson and himself around 1931-33 after Canetti heard them at Bricktop's.","period":"1931-33","year_from":1931,"year_to":1931,"words":276,"start":[270,7],"end":[273,11],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=56679#s45765","tags":{"places":[{"name":"France","focus":0,"type":"country"}],"venues":[{"name":"Bricktop's","focus":0,"city":"Paris"}],"bands":[{"name":"Harlemites","focus":1,"leader":"Freddie Johnson"},{"name":"Bricktop's band","focus":1,"leader":null}]},"people":[{"name":"Booker Pittman","qid":"Q4943194","n":5},{"name":"Freddy Johnson","qid":"Q1408459","n":4},{"name":"Bobby Jones","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Billy Burns","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Bricktop (Ada Smith)","qid":"Q346309","n":2},{"name":"Big Boy Goodie","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Al Castellanos","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Arthur Briggs","qid":"Q708756","n":1},{"name":"Jacques Canetti","qid":"Q1677931","n":1},{"name":"Peter du Conge","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Herb Fleming","qid":"Q1607846","n":1},{"name":"Sterling Conaway","qid":"Q29384813","n":1},{"name":"Billy Taylor","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Juan Fernandez","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Theodore Brock","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Al something","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Alto","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":270,"b":7,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"This was just the Harlemites?"},{"p":270,"b":8,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Yes, the Harlemites."},{"p":270,"b":9,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"And who was in that band?"},{"p":270,"b":10,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"The Harlemites?"},{"p":270,"b":11,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Yes."},{"p":270,"b":12,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"We had --"},{"p":270,"b":13,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Mr. Freddy Johnson."},{"p":270,"b":14,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Freddy Johnson, -- you"},{"p":271,"b":0,"s":"","x":"Briggs 271"},{"p":271,"b":1,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"want the names of them? Yes."},{"p":271,"b":2,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Wait a minute, I'll give them to you."},{"p":271,"b":3,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"This then is the personnel of the Harlemites."},{"p":271,"b":4,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Freddy Johnson, Arthur Briggs, Bobby Jones --"},{"p":271,"b":5,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Playing what?"},{"p":271,"b":6,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Bobby Jones, second trumpet."},{"p":271,"b":7,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Second trumpet."},{"p":271,"b":8,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Theodore Brock, third trumpet. Peter Du Conge, first saxophone, clarinet. Big Boy Goodie, tenor. Al Castellanos, third saxophone. Billy Burns, replacing Herb Harry Fleming who was ill. Sterling Conaway on the guitar."},{"p":271,"b":9,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"What did Burns play?"},{"p":271,"b":10,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"The bass player was Juan Fernandez, a Puerto Rican."},{"p":271,"b":11,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Right."},{"p":272,"b":0,"s":"","x":"Briggs"},{"p":272,"b":1,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Billy Taylor, on drums."},{"p":272,"b":2,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Then we made a couple of replacements. We had Booker Washington -- Booker Pittman."},{"p":272,"b":3,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Booker Pittman."},{"p":272,"b":4,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Yeh. Booker Pittman from Kansas City, and --"},{"p":272,"b":5,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"And what did he play, Pittman; Booker Pittman?"},{"p":272,"b":6,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"He replaced Castellanos."},{"p":272,"b":7,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"On bass?"},{"p":272,"b":8,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"No, no, on alto."},{"p":272,"b":9,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Alto."},{"p":272,"b":10,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Alto, right."},{"p":272,"b":11,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Sorry."},{"p":272,"b":12,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"And Al -- what's his name, Al something, on tenor, who replaced Big Boy."},{"p":272,"b":13,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Oh, it doesn't make any difference. It will probably come back before"},{"p":273,"b":0,"s":"","x":"Briggs 273"},{"p":273,"b":1,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Fine."},{"p":273,"b":2,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"Okay, so this -- now, you formed -- who actually formed this band?"},{"p":273,"b":3,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Freddy and I. The basis of the -- the nucleus of Bricktop's band, that played at Bricktop's."},{"p":273,"b":4,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"I see."},{"p":273,"b":5,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"So it was built around that Bricktop's --"},{"p":273,"b":6,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Built around Bricktop's band."},{"p":273,"b":7,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"And this was when, in 193 --"},{"p":273,"b":8,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"1931."},{"p":273,"b":9,"s":"MR. COLLIER","x":"'31?"},{"p":273,"b":10,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"'31, '32, somewhere around there, yeh."},{"p":273,"b":11,"s":"MR. BRIGGS","x":"Canetti heard us play at Bricktop's, you see, and he being a member of the Hot Club of France, he saw a commercial business, you see."}]}